  "safetyTitle": "Safety centre",
  "topicMeeting": "Meeting someone new",
  "topicMeetingSub": "Tips, and share live location with a trusted friend",
  "topicMeetingBody": "Meet somewhere public the first time, and get there on your own.\n\nTell a friend where you're going. You can share your live location from any chat for up to an hour.\n\nKeep the conversation in Orbit until you trust someone. Be wary of anyone who rushes you or asks for money.\n\nTrust your gut. It's always okay to leave.",
  "topicTravel": "Travel safety",
  "topicTravelSub": "Safer defaults where being queer is risky",
  "topicTravelBody": "In some countries, same-sex relationships are criminalised. When you travel there, Orbit hides your distance by default and shows a safety notice.\n\nConsider turning on the discreet app icon and app lock before you go.\n\nBe cautious with anyone who asks to meet very quickly or pushes to move the chat elsewhere.",
  "topicHealth": "Sexual health",
  "topicHealthSub": "Testing reminders and local services",
  "topicHealthBody": "Regular testing is part of looking after yourself and your partners. Many people test every three months.\n\nAsk a local clinic about PrEP, PEP and vaccinations.\n\nHealth details on your profile are always optional and private by default.",
  "topicModeration": "Blocking & reporting",
  "topicModerationSub": "How moderation works and what happens next",
  "topicModerationBody": "Blocking is instant and two-way: neither of you will see the other anywhere in Orbit. The other person is never told.\n\nReports go to a human moderator. Reports about minors and threats are reviewed first.\n\nWe may warn, suspend or ban accounts. Safety tools are free for everyone.",
  "getHelp": "Get help now",
  "getHelpTitle": "If you're in danger",
  "getHelpBody": "Call your local emergency number now. When you're safe, block and report the person so our team can act.",
